"The steward, Osric Vane, weighs with a heavy pound and books a tenth that is nearer an eighth."
"Osric pockets the difference in grain, sold at Bramwick; the school above him does not know."
"Aldo's tally sticks, read true, would show Osric took about two hundred pounds too much last year."
"Osric is a mortal clerk, not a mage, and fears his masters more than any village."
